- single_best_test_clean_predictions.jsonl (one evaluation split complete)

Lost: all in-memory cache entries, universal_phrase and prompt_injection evaluation rows.

Code fix applied (runner.py): added disk-based cache persistence via _flush_cache() / _load_cache(). Cache is now written to output_dir/prediction_cache.json after calibration and after each method completes. Future crashes are recoverable by restarting.

Blocker resolution: upgrading OpenAI account to tier 2 (requires $50 cumulative spend + 7-day-old account). Tier 2 RPD = 5,000,000 — eliminates the constraint entirely.

Pending: "skip calibration if profiles.json exists" feature would save ~6,000 calls on V2 restart, but tier 2 upgrade makes this less urgent.

