| experiment | model | n_test | SENTRY vs clean_weighted | SENTRY vs majority_vote |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| V1 (50/50) | gpt-4o-mini | 50 | identical | identical |
| V2 (150/75) | gpt-4o-mini | 75 | identical | identical |
| V2c (50/50) | DeepSeek-R1-7B | 50 | identical | slight diff (style_artifact) |

Consistent conclusion across all three: prompt-only diversity within a single model is insufficient to activate SENTRY's mechanisms. Model diversity is required. This is now supported by three independent runs and is the central empirical claim of my contribution.
